    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d276">

                <pb facs="0475" n="363" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg363"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 27/214–215.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister McCreery to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santo
                                Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-11-23"><hi rendition="#italic">November 23,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 61]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 46, of the 5th ultimo,
                    relative to the constitution of the Dominican Republic promulgated on September
                    9, 1907, I have the honor to inclose for the files of the department a copy of
                    the said constitution from the Official Gazette and a translation.</p>
                <p>The constituent convention convoked by the Congress assembled at Santiago de los
                    Cabelleros on the 20th instant for the reform of this constitution.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fenton R.
                    McCreery.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d276-a1.xml" xpointer="d276-a1"/>
            </div>
